@startuml 27-hid-bringup-sequence
' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Diagram 27: Hardware Bring-Up and Pre-Flight Sequence
' MC-HID-001 §11 — Configuration and Bring-Up Checklist
' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

title "27 — Hardware Bring-Up and Pre-Flight Sequence\nFirst-Time Assembly · Software Config · Pre-Flight Checks  ·  MC-HID-001 §11"

skinparam BackgroundColor #FAFBFC
skinparam DefaultFontColor #1C2334
skinparam DefaultFontSize 10
skinparam TitleFontSize 13
skinparam TitleFontStyle bold
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam RoundCorner 5

skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #D8E8F8
  BorderColor #3D5A80
  BorderThickness 1.5
  FontSize 10
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFE8C0
  DiamondBorderColor #C07000
  DiamondFontSize 9
  ArrowColor #3D5A80
  ArrowFontSize 9
  ArrowFontColor #2A4060
  StartColor #1A3860
  EndColor #1A3860
}

skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFAE8
  BorderColor #C09030
  FontSize 9
}

skinparam swimlane {
  BorderColor #8AA8C8
  TitleFontSize 10
  TitleFontStyle bold
  TitleBackgroundColor #E0EAF8
}

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
' PHASE 1: FIRST-TIME ASSEMBLY  (one-time per unit)
' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════

|First-Time Assembly  (one-time per drone unit)|

start

:Verify board revision and silkscreen
against Holybro datasheet
Confirm ttyTHS1 ↔ Pixhawk UART B
solder-jumper compatibility  [HIF-001];

:Insert MicroSD cards:
  Jetson MicroSD (J7) — OS or log storage
  Pixhawk MicroSD (J8) — PX4 flight logs
Lock both cards fully;

:Install CSI-2 FPC cable:
  Unlock ZIF latch on J2
  Insert IMX219 22-pin FPC (blue side up)
  Press ZIF latch closed
  Verify cable is seated flat;

note right
  Inspect cable insertion carefully.
  Mis-insertion causes no image,
  or damaged FPC.  [HIF-003]
end note

:Verify XT60 polarity on battery cable
(positive = larger pin)
Do NOT connect battery yet;

:Connect bench PSU (current limit 5 A)
to XT60 — verify Jetson boots;

if (Jetson boots to login?) then (yes)
  :Remove bench PSU;
else (no)
  :Check PSU polarity · check 5V_SYS rail
  measure voltage at J1 under load;
  stop
endif

:Mount baseboard on airframe using
4× M3 silicone grommets (shore 40A)
Torque M3 bolts to 0.5 N·m;

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
' PHASE 2: SOFTWARE CONFIGURATION  (one-time per unit)
' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════

|Software Configuration  (one-time per drone unit)|

:Connect USB-C (J4) to host PC
(or connect via console J5 at 115200 bps)
Log in to Jetson;

:Run OS installation scripts
01-install-os.sh through 10-install-networking.sh
Each script: idempotent · set -euo pipefail
Verify each companion smoke test passes;

:Configure Netplan on Jetson
/etc/netplan/01-drone-mc.yaml:
  eth0: 192.168.10.11/24  (MANET)
         192.168.12.1/24  (FCC-internal)
netplan apply;

:Apply Jetson-IO device tree overlay
for IMX219 on CSI port 0:
  sudo /opt/nvidia/jetson-io/jetson-io.py
  Select: 22-pin CSI → IMX219
  Reboot;

:Connect GCS laptop (192.168.10.10)
via MANET radio to drone;

:Open QGroundControl on GCS laptop
Connect to Pixhawk on UDP:14550;

:Set PX4 parameters for HIF-001 serial:
  UXRCE_DDS_CFG  = 102  (UART B)
  UXRCE_DDS_BAUD = 921600
  Save and reboot Pixhawk;

:Set PX4 parameters for HIF-002 Ethernet:
  UXRCE_DDS_AG_IP  = 3232238593  (192.168.12.1)
  UXRCE_DDS_PORT_CFG = 8888
  (Secondary transport — serial is primary);

:Calibrate power monitor:
  BAT1_V_DIV   = (see baseboard silkscreen)
  BAT1_A_PER_V = (see baseboard silkscreen)
  Verify QGC battery display matches
  multimeter reading at XT60;

:Verify HIF-001 serial link:
  ros2 topic hz /fmu/out/vehicle_status
  Expect: ≥ 5 Hz;

if (Hz ≥ 5?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Check: drone-mc-fcc-bridge service active?
  Check: /dev/ttyTHS1 exists?
  Check: PX4 UXRCE_DDS_CFG param correct?;
  stop
endif

:Verify HIF-003 camera:
  gst-launch-1.0 nvarguscamerasrc sensor-id=0
  num-buffers=10 ! fakesink -v
  Expect: no errors · 10 frames;

if (Camera OK?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Check: ZIF latch locked?
  Check: device tree overlay applied?
  Check: /dev/video0 exists?;
  stop
endif

:Run full smoke test suite:
  sudo bash 10b-smoke-test-networking.sh
  All checks must pass;

:Configuration complete — unit ready for flight;

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
' PHASE 3: PRE-FLIGHT CHECKS  (each flight)
' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════

|Pre-Flight Checks  (before each flight)|

:Check battery voltage: > 80% remaining
Verify in QGroundControl;

if (Battery OK?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Charge or swap battery;
  stop
endif

:Inspect CSI-2 FPC cable:
  Visual check — no kinks, bends, or displacement
  ZIF latch — still closed;

:Verify MicroSD seated (Pixhawk)
PX4 SD indicator active;

:Start drone-mc.target:
  systemctl start drone-mc.target
  Wait 30 s for all services to reach active (running);

fork
  :ros2 topic hz /fmu/out/vehicle_status
  Expect: ≥ 5 Hz  [HIF-001];
fork again
  :ping 192.168.10.10
  Expect: < 5 ms RTT  [HIF-004];
fork again
  :ros2 topic hz /camera/image_raw
  Expect: ≥ 15 Hz  [HIF-003];
end fork

if (All three checks pass?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Identify failed check
  Consult HIF section for troubleshooting;
  stop
endif

:Run pre-flight smoke test:
  sudo bash 10b-smoke-test-networking.sh;

if (Smoke test PASS?) then (yes)
  :Pre-flight complete
  Safe to connect flight battery and arm;
  stop
else (no)
  :Investigate failure
  Do NOT arm;
  stop
endif

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
' PHASE 4: POST-FLIGHT
' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════

|Post-Flight  (after each flight)|

start

:Disarm — wait for drone to power down;

fork
  :Inspect CSI-2 FPC cable and J2 connector;
fork again
  :Measure battery cell balance
  (< 100 mV imbalance between cells);
fork again
  :Remove Pixhawk MicroSD
  Copy .ulg flight log to archive;
fork again
  :Archive Jetson journal:
  journalctl --since "1 hour ago"
  > flight_$(date +%Y%m%d%H%M).log;
end fork

:Return to storage
(charge battery if needed for next flight);

stop

@enduml
